WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:04.490
When knitting
traditional double bed jacquard.

2
00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:09.060
The stitch pattern is worked on the main
bed and controlled by the automatic

3
00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:12.460
patterning device,
punch card or electronics.

4
00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:15.900
At the same time,
needles are in work on on the ribber

5
00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:21.740
creating a backing and it covers
any floats from the stitch pattern.

6
00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:24.900
Because the yarn colors are
changed every two rows.

7
00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:30.940
Stripes are formed on the back of the
knitting. To alter the striped effect.

8
00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:33.500
Settings are changed or a special carriage

9
00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:38.180
is used that automatically selects
every other needle on the ribber.

10
00:00:38.210 --> 00:00:44.080
The key is to have an even
number of needles in work.

11
00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:52.460
The needles to slip are
alternated every other row.

12
00:00:52.490 --> 00:00:56.020
On Brother machines,
you'll use the lili buttons.

13
00:00:56.050 --> 00:01:00.620
The official name of these buttons
are the ribber Change knobs.

14
00:01:00.650 --> 00:01:06.240
Silver Singer machines use
a separate bird's eye carriage.

15
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:14.760
Look closely and you can see
the slipped ribber needles.

16
00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:21.050
Something to keep in mind is
that this technique not only changes

17
00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:26.260
the appearance of the backing, but it
also distorts the front of the knitting.

18
00:01:26.290 --> 00:01:31.290
Give it a try with your stitch
pattern to see the results.

19
00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:35.060
Bird's eye backing will also
change the gauge of your knitting.

20
00:01:35.090 --> 00:01:39.240
So if you're going to use birds eye,
be sure to swatch with that technique.

